// mp-rs-add-est -- a same-thread RMW, then a third-thread plain store: the P0982 case.
//
// rmm-zoo: litmus/cpp_memory_model/rs/ -- the release-sequence family, vendored
//   from gonzalobg/cpp_memory_model and checked in the zoo against the
//   per-version C++ cat models (cpp11.cat / cpp17.cat / cpp2w.cat, herd7 7.58).
// Source: ISO/IEC 14882:2011, :2017, :2020 (the [atomics.order] release-sequence
//   definition); Boehm, Giroux & Vafeiadis, P0668R5 "Revising the C++ Memory
//   Model" (2018); Boehm, P0982R1 "Weaken Release Sequences" (2018).
//
// Reference verdicts (herd7 7.58, from the zoo's rs/README.md):
//   C++11 ALLOWS  |  C++17 ALLOWS  |  C++20 FORBIDS
//
// This is one of the two tests that pin the P0982 change, and it is fully
// atomic, so no data race muddies the verdict. Under C++11/17 the release
// sequence survives P2's relaxed store and P0's fetch-add reading 2 writes 3
// still carrying the release, so the reader synchronises. C++20's weakened
// release sequence is broken by the intervening plain store and the stale read
// becomes observable -- forbidden there for the opposite reason: with no
// synchronisation the execution that reaches a = 3 no longer exists.
//
// Upstream condition: exists([x]=3 /\ 1:a=3 /\ 1:b=0); the coherence conjunct
// is recorded here rather than asserted (see ../../README.md).
//
// MoRDor's C++20 allows it. The C++20 FORBIDS above is herd7 under the zoo's
// cpp2w.cat, and not P0982's doing: cpp17.cat already has P0982's release
// sequence and herd7 answers Sometimes under it. cpp2w.cat adds
// acyclic(tecotsb | rb), for tecotsb = ([A];eco;[A])+;sb, from a later draft,
// and that axiom forbids message passing over relaxed accesses too (herd7
// answers MP+rlx Never under it), which no published C++ forbids. MoRDor's C++20
// is cpp17.cat's release sequence with RC11's psc, and agrees with herd7 under
// cpp17.cat.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  y.store(1, rlx);
  x.store(1, rel);
  rpx := &x;
  rt := FADD(rlx, rlx, rpx, 1)
} ||| {
  r1 := x.load(acq);
  if (r1 = 3) {
    r2 := y.load(rlx)
  } else {skip}
} ||| {
  x.store(2, rlx)
}
%%
allow (r1 = 3 && r2 = 0) [C11, C17, C20]
forbid (ub) [C11, C17, C20]
